course: dictionary
lesson: 10955
title: One word, more than one meaning
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A word can have more than one meaning. Look at the words around it to find the one the writer means. «On a path shared with walkers you ring your bell and pass slowly, because people walking may not hear you.» Here a walker is a person who walks, often for fun.
explain: The same word can also mean a frame that helps someone who cannot walk well, or a baby, to walk. A dog walker is a person paid to take dogs for walks. «Do not forget the people when you count legs: a dog walker with 4 dogs makes 2 + 4 × 4 = 18 legs.» Here the dog walker is a person, so the person's legs count too.
fact: A walker is a person who walks, often for fun or sport.
fact: A walker can also be a frame that helps a person who cannot walk well, or a baby, to walk.
fact: A dog walker is a person paid to take dogs for walks.
fact: Walkers on country roads face the traffic and should wear bright clothes.
fact: «If cattle chase a walker with a dog, the walker should let go of the lead so both can get away.»
exercise: «On a path shared with walkers you ring your bell and pass slowly.» Who are the walkers? | A road with cars on it | *People who walk, often for fun | A frame that helps someone walk | A dog paid to go for a walk
exercise: Read: «a dog walker with 4 dogs». What is a dog walker? | A person who never leaves the house | *A person paid to take dogs for walks | A dog that walks very fast | A frame that helps dogs stand up
exercise: Which phrase means a frame that helps someone who cannot walk well? | Walkers in the park | *A walker frame | A fast walker | A sponsored walk
test: «Walkers in England crossed a field with cows and their calves.» In this sentence, walkers means | cows that run fast | a frame to help walking | calves | *people who walk
test: What should a walker do if cattle chase them with a dog? | Shout at the cows | Run back to the village | *Let go of the lead so both can get away | Keep the lead tight and stand still
exam: «A London footbridge wobbled on its first day in 2000 because walkers fell into step with its sway.» Which meaning of walkers fits here? | Cows in a field | Dogs taken for walks | *People who walk | Frames that help a person walk
